:[[0,false],[24350,true]],"p":1.0,"show":[[0,false],[24350,true]],"type":"packet","x1":20.0,"x2":80.0,"y1":81.0,"y2":81.0},{"label":"6c:e2:41:9a:b7","p":[[25400,0.0],[26599,1.0]],"show":[[0,false],[25400,true],[26600,false]],"type":"packet","x1":80.0,"x2":20.0,"y1":90.0,"y2":90.0},{"label":"6c:e2:41:9a:b7","landed":[[0,false],[27350,true]],"p":1.0,"show":[[0,false],[27350,true]],"type":"packet","x1":80.0,"x2":20.0,"y1":90.0,"y2":90.0},{"dim":[[0,true]],"left":true,"text":[[0,"ClientHello + key share"],[5200,"ServerHello + certificate + key share"],[10400,"both sides derive the session key"],[15600,"Finished (encrypted)"],[21650,"encrypted application data"]],"type":"text","x":2.0,"y":6.0},{"left":false,"text":"g = 5, p = 23 · public","type":"text","x":50.0,"y":14.0},{"left":false,"text":"a = 6 · private, never sent","type":"text","x":20.0,"y":24.0},{"dim":[[0,true],[5200,false]],"left":false,"text":"b = 15 · private, never sent","type":"text","x":80.0,"y":24.0},{"left":false,"show":[[0,false],[11500,true]],"text":"Bᵃ = 19⁶ mod 23 = 2 · key","type":"text","x":20.0,"y":30.0},{"left":false,"show":[[0,false],[11500,true]],"text":"Aᵇ = 8¹⁵ mod 23 = 2 · key","type":"text","x":80.0,"y":30.0}],"header":"INTERACTIVE · TLS ·· THE HANDSHAKE","note":[[0,"Browser picks a private number a = 6, keeps it, and sends ClientHello: the ciphers it supports plus share A = 5⁶ mod 23 = 8. Getting a back from 8 is the discrete logarithm problem, infeasible at real sizes."],[5200,"Server picks its own private number b = 15 and replies with its chosen cipher, share B = 5¹⁵ mod 23 = 19, and its certificate; the share is signed with the certificate's key, so a machine in the middle cannot swap in a share of its own."],[10400,"Each side raises the share it received to its own private number: 19⁶ mod 23 = 2 in the browser, 8¹⁵ mod 23 = 2 on the server. Same value, the session key, and the wire carried only 8 and 19."],[15600,"Each side sends Finished, the first message protected by the new key. Watch the key work: encrypted at the sender, ciphertext on the wire, decrypted with the same key on arrival."],[21650,"Every packet from here on gets the same treatment, encrypted with the session key before leaving, decrypted with it on arrival. This is HTTPS."]]}